rns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"blind_id\":\"ST056\",\"coverage\":[{\"point\":1,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"The answer covers all three inquiry areas. Selection: 'Why this exchange and lead market maker (LMM)?', alternatives evaluated, criteria and conflicts. Relevant-market expertise: experience with comparable ETFs and their underlying markets. Capital/seed: 'Who supplies launch capital, how much, on what terms, and when may it exit?'\"},{\"point\":2,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"It separates the two kinds of assets: 'Temporary market-maker seed facilitates launch and trading; it is not evidence of durable investor demand.' It does not treat investor assets as permanent. It says to assess their 'concentration and likely persistence.'\"}],\"central_error\":null,\"local_error\":null,\"grade\":\"correct\",\"rationale\":\"Both required minimums are fully covered. The answer frames the checklist as 'Suggested board inquiries—not mandatory approval conditions.' It never says market-maker seed is guaranteed or permanent, and it never says a fixed capital amount is legally required. It also asks when launch capital may exit and what happens if support disappears. No central error and no material local falsehood.\"}","ttft_ms":3243,"type":"result","duration_ms":6589,"uuid":"7c163a37-3a63-4df7-9489-0815225e9254","ttft_stream_ms":1070,"time_to_request_ms":54,"first_content_frame_ms":1070,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
